<title>USA: Moody's says it not planning to cut Italy ratings.</title>
<headline>Moody's says it not planning to cut Italy ratings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service Inc is not considering downgrading the Aa3 country ceiling and government bond ratings of Italy, Vincent Truglia, managing director of the rating agency's sovereign risk unit in New York, said Friday.  </p>
<p>Truglia added, &quot;Both ratings are stable at the current time.&quot;</p>
<p>He was responding to rumors that a credit-rating agency planned to cut Italy's ratings.</p>
<p>Moody's raised Italy's country ceiling and government bond ratings to Aa3 from A1 in July 1996, Truglia said.</p>
<p>((--Douglas Brown, U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1662))</p>
